Add a Rank column to Table 1

Rank is global across all 15 system configurations, ordered by Avg, not
per-group. The rows stay split into closed-source and open-weight, so
the ranks run non-monotonically within each block — which is the point:
it shows Lychee-FD at 4 ahead of Grok, both GPT-Realtime configs and
everything below them.

Standard competition ranking, so the 3.2 tie between Grok Voice and
Moshi-RL shares rank 8 and the next rank is 10. Ranks are derived from
the Avg cells rather than written by hand.

Alignment now keys off .rank and .model classes instead of :first-child,
which would otherwise have left-aligned the rank numbers and the second
header row's "Spk." cell.

